  "surprise": "P02 follow-up: RMS-matched Muon update scaling (shape factor sqrt(max(rows,cols)/256) instead of sqrt(max(1,rows/cols)); only the (256,1024) fc2 step doubles) on incumbent 070-claude scored 402/340/325 on seeds 0/1/2 versus 359/335/364: exact means 355.67 versus 352.67, +3.0 (+0.9%); paired +43/+5/-39. Keep under the strictly-higher three-seed rule (rounded 356 vs 353); no other-agent result was published during the run, so 070-claude was the bar. Read it as a tie inside seed noise, not an established effect: the seed spread widened (325-402 vs 335-364) and the keep rests on seed 0, whose 402 is the highest single-seed score so far. Pretraining matched the prediction: 4782/4706/4711 steps (070: 4784/4750/4776), final val loss 0.0909/0.0918/0.0961 versus 0.0911/0.0913/0.0961, held-out greedy 0.987/0.990/0.988. The registered mechanism signature failed on every seed: round-1 targets solved 183/145/141 versus 070's 200/324/206, so stronger MLP writes did not give a better starting policy. Where a gain appeared it came late: RL-solved after round 4 was 852/769/728 versus 788/783/838, and seed 2 started slowly (round-2 accuracy 0.123 vs 0.269, 259 vs 534 solved) before adding 469 proofs in round 4. fc2 weight norms were not logged, so whether its scale actually rose 1.4-2x is unmeasured. Net: fc2's Muon step size is flat for Stage-1 fit and roughly neutral downstream.",
